10 ∈ O(1)

Question 4

Algorithm A:
8n²
Algorithm B:
64n log(n)

To find when Algorithm A beats Algorithm B:
8n² < 64n log(n)
Divide both sides by 8n:
n < 8log(n)
Testing values (assuming log base 2):
For n = 32:
32 < 8log₂(32)
32 < 40 ✓
For n = 64:
64 < 8log₂(64)
64 < 48 ✗
Therefore, the crossover point is between 32 and 64.
Approximate value:
n ≈ 43

Algorithm A beats Algorithm B when n is approximately less than 43.
For larger values of n, Algorithm B is more efficient because O(n log n) grows slower than O(n²).
